 2. 📕 Word of the year 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios Dictionary.com named "maxxing" its 2026 Word of the Year, Axios' Josephine Walker reports . 

 The word's explosive popularity reflects society's relentless drive to optimize everything. Dictionary Media Group director of lexicography Steve Johnson tells Axios that maxxing was an ideal pick because it's endlessly adaptable.

 Fitness enthusiasts are "proteinmaxxing," AI superfans are "tokenmaxxing" and the Trump administration says it's "deportationmaxxing." Read the announcement . 

 
 
